  "fallbacksAbout": "Metric-matched fallback faces, in order: each is the family name '<Family> Fallback' (then ' B', ' C') over local() fonts with the same metrics (Arimo and Liberation Sans match Arial, Gelasio matches Georgia, Cousine and Liberation Mono match Courier New). The B and C faces cover systems with only DejaVu (Linux containers, headless browsers): size-adjust is the ratio of the web font's to the local font's average advance on English text, measured in Chromium; ascent and descent are the web font's (Public Sans 0.950/0.225 em, Newsreader 0.735/0.265 em, Martian Mono 1.000/0.200 em) divided by size-adjust. Public Sans C (DejaVu Serif) is for systems with no sans-serif font at all, where the browser would fall back to a serif anyway."
